// register: APB4SLVADDRESSBLOCK.DMACH1_CH_CMD
/* desc: Channel DMA Command Register

This register allows the SW to control the operation of a DMA command.*/
                
/* field: APB4SLVADDRESSBLOCK.DMACH1_CH_CMD.ENABLECMD, pos: [0:0] -- Channel Enable. When set to '1', enables the channel to run its programmed task. When set to '1', it cannot be set back to zero, and this field will automatically clear to zero when a DMA process is completed. To force the DMA to stop prematurely, you must use CH_CMD.STOPCMD instead.*/
