/* field: DWC_DDRPHYA_MASTER0_P0.SEQ0BDLY0_P0.SEQ0BDLY0_P0, pos: [15:0] -- PHY Initialization Engine (PIE) Delay Register 0.
This register is available for selection by the NOP and WAIT instructions
in the PIE for the delay value.
Programmed by dwc_ddrphy_phyinit_I_loadPIEImage() to support frequency changes.

Programming Seq0BDLY[3,2,1,0] Registers:
 - These registers are used to control various delays during PLL, DLL initialization.
 - These registers should be programmed with the corresponding number of MEMCLK cycles representing a fixed amount of delay irrespective of DfiClk Frequency.
 - When calculating the number of cycles to be programmed for each PState, it should be noted that the sequencer multiplies programmed values by a factor of 8 and values are round down to the closest integer.

Register | Required Delay | Programmed Value 
 - Seq0BDLY0 | 0.5us | ( 0.5us / MEMCLK period) / 8)
 - Seq0BDLY1 | 1.0us | ( 1.0us / MEMCLK period) / 8)
 - Seq0BDLY2 | 10.0us | (10.0us / MEMCLK period) / 8)
 - Seq0BDLY2 | 10.0us | 64/4 if (MEMCLK Freq <= 400MHz)
 - Seq0BDLY3 | - | 132/4 if (400MHz Freq < MEMCLK Freq <= 533MHz)
 - Seq0BDLY3 | - | 176/4 if (MEMCLK Freq > 533MHz)*/
