/* field: DWC_DDRPHYA_MASTER0_P0.MAPCAA0TODFI.MAPCAA0TODFI, pos: [3:0] -- For LPDDR3 and LPDDR4 applications, these CSRs map a dfi0_address to CAA 0.

Unused for DDR3 and unused for DDR4 applications.
Each register in the set of MapCAAtoDfi must have a unique value within the set.

For example, if PHY CAA0 is mapped from dfi0_address[2], then Register MapCAA0toDfi should be 2.
 - LPDDR4 ACX3,ACX6,ACX10,ACX12 registers MapCAA[0..5]toDfi are used
 -- values 0-5 are valid,
 -- values 6-15 are reserved
 -- registers MapCAA[6..9]toDfi are reserved
 - LPDDR3 ACX3: not supported
 - LPDDR3 ACX6,ACX10,ACX12: registers MapCAA[0..9]toDfi are used
 -- values 0-9 are valid,
 -- values 10-15 are reserved
 - LPDDR3 ACX6,ACX10,ACX12: registers MapCAA[0..9]toDfi are used
 -- values 0-9 are valid,
 -- values 10-15 are reserved*/
